findings.description:
The protocol does not specify three things:
- whether the querying agent appears in its own result;
- whether the radius boundary is inclusive;
- the order of returned indices.

Slice 105 must show behavioural output "identical before and after the swap". Floating-point force sums depend on order, so a spatial hash returning the same set in a different order would not be bit-identical. Specify ascending index order, self-inclusion and boundary rule here, and assert them in `test_spatial.py`.
